claim.claim-text:
acquiring an image of a scene;
identifying a plurality of objects in the image;
classifying the plurality of identified objects, wherein a first plurality of identified objects is classified as stationary objects, and a second plurality of identified objects is classified as any of suspicious, non-stationary, or suspicious and non-stationary objects;
determining if respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects are available;
in response to the respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects being not available, passively measuring the respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects;
actively measuring respective distances to the second plurality of identified objects; and
fusing the respective passively measured distances of the first plurality of identified objects and the respective actively measured distances of the second plurality of identified objects to generate the 3D map.

comparing the to a previously acquired image;
identifying changes in locations of the first plurality of objects based on the comparison; and
classifying the first plurality of objects as stationary objects based on the identified changes in locations of the first plurality of objects.

generating a predication image based the acquired image, wherein the predication image illustrating predicted positions of the plurality of objects;
acquiring a subsequent image;
determining if there are any differences between locations for the plurality of objects; and
in response to no difference exists between locations for the first plurality of objects, classifying the first plurality of identified objects as stationary objects.

for each of the first plurality of identified objects,
estimating an approximate size;
estimating an amount of pixels occupy in the image; and
determining the respective distance based on the approximate size and the amount of pixels.

identify a plurality of objects in the image;
classify the plurality of identified objects, wherein a first plurality of identified objects is classified as stationary objects, and a second plurality of identified objects is classified as any of suspicious, non-stationary, or suspicious and non-stationary objects;
determine if respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects are available;
in response to the respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects being not available, the passive sensor further configured to passively measure the respective distances of the first plurality of identified objects;
an active sensor configured to actively measure respective distances to the second plurality of identified objects; and
the processing system further configured to:
fuse the respective passively measured distances of the first plurality of identified objects and the respective actively measured distances of the second plurality of identified objects to generate the 3D map.

comparing the to a previously acquired image;
identifying changes in locations of the first plurality of objects based on the comparison; and
classifying the first plurality of objects as stationary objects based on the identified changes in locations of the first plurality of objects.

estimate an approximate size;
estimate an amount of pixels occupy in the image; and
determine the respective distance based on the approximate size and the amount of pixels.
